#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514526} :activity/id #uuid "627cdea7-e74f-570d-9499-4dfeee52d335" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048491 :topic/id #uuid "a4553111-5fc5-5a4e-8071-e4805050c5b5" :topic/math-academy-id 3069} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514496 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514389 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1faf8fac-95d9-5c9b-afb5-041607bd6022" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2.602" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513616} {:answer/id #uuid "4e0d5475-2c71-5b00-9cf3-9aedb6ecd6ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.341" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513744} {:answer/id #uuid "59e0ee7f-17c9-57f5-a020-609a22fffdf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2.131" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513773} {:answer/id #uuid "7d78c7b2-e987-5f4d-ba6c-f50a26e8560e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.337" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513859} {:answer/id #uuid "88cbab98-0bfd-5b51-8738-97197bbd173d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2.567" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513888}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513616} :answer-field/id #uuid "faac0f2c-9586-5270-b3d8-5b3c6c767d29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3619ef06-3622-5375-8459-4e89f07dd7d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-142722" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X$ has a student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom. Given that the random variable $X∼{T}_{15},$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(|X|\\ge x)=0.02.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $15$ | $1.341$ | $1.753$ | $2.131$ | $2.602$ | $2.947$ |\n| $16$ | $1.337$ | $1.746$ | $2.120$ | $2.583$ | $2.921$ |\n| $17$ | $1.333$ | $1.740$ | $2.110$ | $2.576$ | $2.898$ |" :question/worked-solution "![](images/63/635de7075b0d106ffc2a0f15e65ca7a3406a49945591aa5eae59090c74df1398.png)\n\nDue to the symmetry of the student's $t$-distribution, we have that $P(|X|\\ge x)=0.02$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\n2P(X\\ge x)=0.02\\,⟹\\,P(X\\ge x)=0.01.\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{T}_{15},$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=15.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $15$ | $1.341$ | $1.753$ | $2.131$ | $2.602$ | $2.947$ |\n| $16$ | $1.337$ | $1.746$ | $2.120$ | $2.583$ | $2.921$ |\n| $17$ | $1.333$ | $1.740$ | $2.110$ | $2.567$ | $2.898$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 2.602)=0.010.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=2.602.$"} :step/id #uuid "3021eda6-e3b8-5219-817c-73b31f6cb117" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514505}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514503 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514403 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d5a030c-04ff-5537-a509-3d205630e231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2.779" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513692} {:answer/id #uuid "42153ec8-896b-5a88-a532-420303c9dfdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.708" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513708} {:answer/id #uuid "a3e04a1f-348f-5bb3-a5be-0930d2f13a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.318" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513953} {:answer/id #uuid "ec242ef5-dc63-533d-8db7-e947ec25bdd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2.787" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514151} {:answer/id #uuid "fcc85b2f-6e5e-5e04-b574-f8f024c0b55e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2.485" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514193}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514151} :answer-field/id #uuid "885ef5b5-44d7-500b-bb70-819519766275" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514292}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "53bedfc9-6dd3-5f58-8bd9-2e76db557744" :question/math-academy-id "q-142580" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X$ has a student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom. Given that the random variable $X∼{T}_{25},$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X\\le x)=0.995.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $24$ | $1.318$ | $1.711$ | $2.064$ | $2.492$ | $2.797$ |\n| $25$ | $1.316$ | $1.708$ | $2.060$ | $2.485$ | $2.787$ |\n| $26$ | $1.315$ | $1.706$ | $2.056$ | $2.479$ | $2.779$ |" :question/worked-solution "The table shows probabilities in the form $P(X\\ge x).$ So first, we express the desired probability in this form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge x) & =1-P(X\\le x) \\\\  & =1-0.995 \\\\  & =0.005\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{T}_{25},$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=25.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $24$ | $1.318$ | $1.711$ | $2.064$ | $2.492$ | $2.797$ |\n| $25$ | $1.316$ | $1.708$ | $2.060$ | $2.485$ | $2.787$ |\n| $26$ | $1.315$ | $1.706$ | $2.056$ | $2.479$ | $2.779$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 2.787)=0.005.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=2.787.$"} :step/id #uuid "54c28814-14fa-5e14-be7b-d99db191689b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514496}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514505 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514439 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02dbcaed-89eb-5fb0-b72c-f9dd1752a026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.708" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513534} {:answer/id #uuid "5b781a62-5301-58de-9505-2d037b1f3